type: dataset
title: "Eulogikon: Ancient Greek Texts Corpus"
abstract: "The surviving literary works of ancient Greece in clean, structured, readable form. 1,358 authors and 4,060 works (≈44 million words) spanning Homer through late antiquity — epic, lyric, philosophy, history, drama, medicine, mathematics, rhetoric, and the fragmentary traditions. Published as PDF, Markdown, and plain text. The ancient Greek source texts are Public Domain Mark 1.0; Eulogikon's scaffolding is CC0-1.0."
